title: "The Tribe in the Machine"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Baird
    given-names: Michael L.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-4580-1749"
date-released: 2026-11-15
version: "1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/michaelbaird/tribe-in-the-machine"
url: "https://mikebaird.substack.com/p/the-tribe-in-the-machine"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  An essay and experiment on whether frontier AI models change their answers depending on the
  asker's stated religious identity (devout Christian, committed atheist, or none), across God,
  immigration, same-sex marriage, and a standing-desk control (900 answers, five models, three
  LLM judges plus side-by-side checks), followed by a five-model debate that produced the
  consensus essay. Written by Michael L. Baird with contributions from GPT-6.1 Sol, Claude
  Opus 5.5, Gemini 4 Argon, Grok 4.7, and DeepSeek V4 Pro. No human audit was performed.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - sycophancy
  - religion
  - belief
  - identity
